Part of #64599. `11.0.100-rc.2.26504.105`; the same behaviour on RC 1.

One Minimal API endpoint taking a union that the structural classifier refuses (`JsonUnionTypeStructuralClassifier`, #129805) makes endpoint building throw. The request then returns 500 for **every** route in the app, including routes that don't use the union:

```csharp
public record NotRequired;
public record PendingApproval;
public record PartlyApproved(Guid Approver);
[JsonUnion(TypeClassifier = typeof(JsonUnionTypeStructuralClassifier))]
public union Approval(NotRequired, PendingApproval, PartlyApproved);

app.MapGet("/ok", () => "ok");
app.MapPost("/x", (Approval a) => a);
// GET /ok => 500 NotSupportedException: The JsonUnionTypeStructuralClassifier cannot classify
//   union type 'Approval' because the case type 'NotRequired' can never be selected uniquely...
```

The throw comes from `RouteEndpointDataSource.CreateRouteEndpointBuilder` / `get_Endpoints()`.

| Setup | Result |
|---|---|
| Minimal API only | startup succeeds; every route 500 on the first request |
| `AddControllers()` plus the bad Minimal API endpoint | `StartAsync` throws `NotSupportedException` |
| `AddAuthorization()` | startup throws |
| The bad union only on an MVC action | only that action fails (500); `/ok` and other MVC routes return 200 |
| A union ambiguous only at read time (no classifier) | only that endpoint fails (400) |

The structural classifier rejecting indistinguishable cases is by design (#129805). The question is the scope of the failure. Is it intended that one such endpoint takes the whole endpoint table down on Minimal APIs, or should the exception be scoped to that endpoint, as MVC already does?

Probes: `QOa` and `Probe2` section G in https://github.com/robertodalmonte/csharp-unions-probed

